Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||05-26-2001||02:45 PM||||Trying to switch my battery to the front mount (already made my case, cut out the hole,created a cardboard mold and glassed it, then painted it) Its very solid & looks pretty good.   But now the problem.. I cant find any cables long enough here.. <P>I did find  a set of Booster cables (6gauge 20feet long for $20 Canadian) <P>Will they work if I put them inside the plastic pipe I am putting  under the car?<P>Is there any difference in quality, etc to 6 gauge battery cables vs 6 gauge booster cables?<P>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||William Federle||05-26-2001||03:01 PM||||You can get a 25 foot long #2 red or black battery cable from JC Whitney for about $29.00.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||05-26-2001||06:15 PM||||Well, I guess I was wrong about JC Whitney having #2 cable. However Summit Racing has it. Go to this link and battery boxes, trays, and equipment, and then select battery cable kit. It's around $24.00 for a 20 foot piece of red #2, a three foot piece of black #2, and some hardware.<BR> <A HREF="http://store.summitracing.com/default.asp?target=Department.asp?d=11" TARGET=_blank>http://store.summitracing.com/default.asp?target=Department.asp?d=11</A> <p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 05-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||05-26-2001||06:17 PM||||Any welding or maybe farm supply store should have #2 cable on the roll.  Princess Auto has it here in Ottawa, so they should in Dartmouth too.<BR>Gary<BR>UPEI Class of 75||||reg||14
Z||000004||Phil||05-26-2001||06:35 PM||||A boating supply store has such cable on a roll.||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||05-26-2001||07:25 PM||||Go to a welding supply.Welding cable is very flexible.You can use garden hose or something similar to protect it from any sharp objects under the car.||||reg||1
